     5	| Area | Status | Evidence and observed boundary |
     6	|---|---|---|
     7	| Interactive turns and inference | Implemented | `AutonomousAgent.runTurn` delegates to `runTurnImpl` ([agent.ts:4186](../../cli/src/agent.ts#L4186), [run_turn.ts:26](../../cli/src/core/run_turn.ts#L26)); provider recovery and context admission are in the turn path. `TurnResult` distinguishes interrupted, blocked and failed executions and requires evidence for verified outcomes ([turn.ts:17](../../cli/src/core/turn.ts#L17), [turn.ts:423](../../cli/src/core/turn.ts#L423)). |
     8	| Transient delegation | Implemented, incomplete | `runSubagent` is an in-turn child path ([agent.ts:4463](../../cli/src/agent.ts#L4463)); the model tool is registered through the capability spine ([spine_handlers.ts:441](../../cli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts#L441)). Result type is only `{completed, summary, reason?, needsInput?}` ([agent_support.ts:35](../../cli/src/core/agent_support.ts#L35)); no shared typed delegation contract, authority-intersection record or recursive child graph is present in that type. Existing delegation coverage includes `agt111_subagent_parity.test.ts`, `team_convergence.test.ts`, `vc9_subagent_needs_input.test.ts` and convergence invariants.
     9	| Durable work units and scheduling | Implemented | `newOperation` constructs operation state and enforces unit invariants and cycle detection ([operation.ts:489](../../cli/src/core/operation.ts#L489), [operation.ts:559](../../cli/src/core/operation.ts#L559)); `ConvergenceScheduler` selects transitions ([scheduler.ts:53](../../cli/src/core/scheduler.ts#L53)); `driveOperation` and `OperationStore` persist and resume work ([operation_runner.ts:717](../../cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts#L717), [operation_runner_persistence.ts:28](../../cli/src/core/operation_runner_persistence.ts#L28)). Existing tests cover schema, restart, concurrency and isolated integration.
    10	| Roles and independent review | Implemented, incomplete | Specialist profiles define permitted tools, read-only declarations, inputs, ceilings and output contracts ([specialist_profiles.ts:22](../../cli/src/core/specialist_profiles.ts#L22)); operation roles include team and specialist profiles ([roles.ts:101](../../cli/src/core/roles.ts#L101)). Independent-review formatting and verdict validation exist ([independent_review.ts:131](../../cli/src/core/independent_review.ts#L131), [independent_review.ts:204](../../cli/src/core/independent_review.ts#L204)); source presence does not establish all requested independence dimensions or reviewer behavior under truncated evidence.
    11	| Resource and provider handling | Implemented, incomplete | `ResourceRegistry` handles eligibility and provider conditions ([resources.ts:194](../../cli/src/core/resources.ts#L194)); provider capability states include `unknown` and `unavailable` ([provider_capabilities.ts:26](../../cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts#L26)); recovery classification/controller exists ([provider_recovery.ts:96](../../cli/src/core/provider_recovery.ts#L96), [provider_recovery.ts:367](../../cli/src/core/provider_recovery.ts#L367)). Provider test sources include `provider_wire_matrix.test.ts`, `provider_capabilities.test.ts`, `provider_robustness.test.ts`, `cloud_providers.test.ts` and `provider_recovery.test.ts`; this assignment's complete workflow has not been run against the requested minimal contract fixture.
    12	| `/team` and operation CLI | Implemented, incomplete | `TeamOrchestrator` maps roles to durable work units ([team.ts:43](../../cli/src/team.ts#L43), [team.ts:126](../../cli/src/team.ts#L126)); the operation CLI accepts validated JSON work-unit specs ([operation_cli.ts:88](../../cli/src/operation_cli.ts#L88)). The REPL has a dedicated `/team` handler ([repl.ts:1688](../../cli/src/repl.ts#L1688)); the sidecar routes commands through a separate slash router ([sidecar.ts:890](../../cli/src/sidecar.ts#L890), [router.ts:14](../../cli/src/slash/router.ts#L14)). TUI completion/help comes from the slash catalogue, with remote invocation parsing in Rust ([catalog.ts:93](../../cli/src/slash/catalog.ts#L93), [slash.rs:25](../../core/src/bin/nexus_tui/slash.rs#L25)).
    13	| `/loop`, `/goal`, `/batch` | Unimplemented as command lifecycles | No command entries or handlers exist in the current slash catalogue/handlers or REPL. `loop_patterns.test.ts` and `nonprogress_recovery.test.ts` test agent-loop detection; neither implements a durable `/loop` controller. The objective ledger is available through `runTurn` and `/requirements`, but there is no `/goal` lifecycle controller. There is no `/batch` command; existing operation JSON work-unit specs are a compatible starting format.
    14	| Pause, cancellation and restart | Implemented, incomplete | The operation runner attaches abort signals and persists cancellation ([operation_runner.ts:127](../../cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts#L127)); `CANCELLED` is terminal in the runner ([operation_runner.ts:142](../../cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts#L142)), while resume explicitly changes a cancelled operation back to running ([operation_cli.ts:325](../../cli/src/operation_cli.ts#L325)). There is no distinct paused status. An operation interruption can also leave an unknown execution outcome; current work-unit recovery is bounded, but `/loop` and `/batch` reconciliation semantics are absent.
    15	| Skills and authority | Implemented, incomplete | Skill activation has constraints and content digests ([skill_activation.ts:67](../../cli/src/core/skill_activation.ts#L67), [skill_activation.ts:104](../../cli/src/core/skill_activation.ts#L104)). Capability registration exists ([capabilities.ts:120](../../cli/src/core/capabilities.ts#L120)) and the orchestration capability schema declares `spawn_subagent` ([orchestration.ts:38](../../cli/src/core/capability_definitions/orchestration.ts#L38)). Full effect-path mediation and path-scoped profile/skill eligibility still require adversarial tests from the assignment.
    16	
    17	## Roadmap and compatibility notes
    18	
    19	- v1.3 PA-1, PA-2 and PA-3 already cover parallel visibility, verified integration and goal semantics. PA-4 stages this assignment against those units and the active WP-P10-02 durable-budget work.
    20	- Operation records are versioned and reject records from a newer schema ([operation_schema.ts:26](../../cli/src/core/operation_schema.ts#L26), [operation_schema.ts:59](../../cli/src/core/operation_schema.ts#L59)). Lifecycle additions must use that migration gate rather than reinterpret old records.
    21	- XERJ definition-first lookup identified `TeamOrchestrator`, `WorkUnitSpec`, `newOperation` and the existing dependency-cycle check. The first batch-spec package reuses the operation parser and constructor; no orchestration code was copied.
    22	- No provider, gateway, or homelab-ai change is part of the workstream.
